(a) The board of commissioners of the county shall continue to be the chief executive entity of the county, and it shall be the duty of the board to set the overall executive policies and procedures of the county. The county manager shall be the chief administrative officer of the county and shall be responsible to the board for the proper and efficient administration of all the affairs of the county except as otherwise provided by law. In addition it shall be the duty of the county manager to:
(1) To maintain a qualified and competent workforce by developing and maintaining a comprehensive personnel system. The county manager shall be responsible for insuring that the county recruits and retains qualified and competent employees to fulfill the various positions throughout the county. To this extent, the county manager shall be responsible for developing and maintaining a job description that identifies the duties, responsibilities, and educational requirements of each county position. The county manager shall have the authority to remove all department heads which the board of commissioners have been heretofore empowered to discharge with the exception of the road superintendent, county attorney, county engineer, and the outside auditor who shall be appointed and removed by the board of commissioners. Although the county manager has the authority to remove department heads, the board of commissioners shall retain the authority to appoint the department heads based on the county managers' recommendations. The county manager shall confirm department head appointments and discharge in accordance with established county policies;
(2) To be in charge of preparing and advertising for applications for department head positions and recommending a shortlist to the board of commissioners for their appointment;
(3) To be in charge of disciplinary actions according to the county personnel policy for all department heads and employees in the county commission office;
(4) To insure that the policies, procedures, and directives issued by the board of commissioners are adhered to in the day-to-day operations of the county;
(5) To exercise control over all departments or divisions of the county which the board has heretofore exercised or that may hereafter be created;
(6) To submit a proposed annual budget to the board of commissioners for their review, input, changes, and approval;
(7) To keep the board of commissioners fully advised as to the financial condition and needs of said county;
(8) To supervise and direct the official conduct of all county officers and department heads;
(9) To attend all meetings of the board with the right to take part in the discussion provided he or she shall have no vote before the board;
(10) To perform such other duties as may be required by the board.
(Ord. of 7-7-2015, § C)

